270
00:16:47,740 --> 00:16:49,820
May we be partners of it.

271
00:16:50,300 --> 00:17:00,220
The best illustration, the best human illustration I think we have for this three-tenths salvation is that of adoption, right?

272
00:17:00,220 --> 00:17:09,400
Think about an orphan on the streets with no one but themselves, no resources, no family structure, no help, no support.

273
00:17:09,480 --> 00:17:25,340
In a moment, in an instant, a loving father invites that orphan to come into their home, to be accepted into their family, to be welcomed with all of the legal rights and status of being a child of that family.

274
00:17:25,540 --> 00:17:27,740
That is a past tense experience.

275
00:17:27,740 --> 00:17:29,900
Some of you in the room, you've done this, right?

276
00:17:29,900 --> 00:17:35,940
You've sat in a courtroom and watched the judge hit the gavel and say, this child is now legally a part of your family.

277
00:17:35,940 --> 00:17:38,480
That is past tense salvation.

278
00:17:38,480 --> 00:17:39,620
A moment.

279
00:17:39,620 --> 00:17:41,200
You've been brought into the family.

